# ONE Genesis v066 — Across All Connected ONE App Sources

**Nathan Tabor · ONE → TABOR ROOT → TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY**

## Shared installation

ONE v061 already provides a shared opt-in system drawer to 54 public browser pages. Four native-web HTML resource pages in SSS-CS and Stewie & Mr. Finn use local copies of the same loader. v066 adds the same additive Genesis extension to all three source-loader locations.

- Shared public file: `app-factory/shared/one-genesis-v066.js`
- SSS-CS local copy: `app-factory/sss-cs/ios/SSSCS/Web/one-genesis-v066.js`
- Stewie & Mr. Finn local copy: `app-factory/stewie-mr-finn/Resources/PolarMiddleC/one-genesis-v066.js`

## Operations

NOTHING (empty visible view), SOMETHING (one named record), ANYTHING (a chosen catalog record), EVERYTHING (the eight explicitly declared template records). Supports 4×4=16 operations, a dual view, the seven-command operation sequence, Undo, Reset, and explicit JSON export.

The original owner's seven statements are preserved **verbatim only in the private ONE v065–v066 archive**, including repetitions. Do not substitute a generated version for the private manuscript.

## Scope and protection

This is a browser/session-level demonstration, not a rewrite of other apps' databases. Actions never write to original apps or external services. Source-level inclusion across 58 app entry points does not certify live browser delivery, native signing, installed apps, backend connections, or syncing. Four native-web resource pages require a signed iOS rebuild before device behavior is verified.

No private books, photos, customer data, secrets, bank records, or unpublished research are included. Nothing is run until the user selects a control. Saved prior work is not overwritten.
